# Static-asset response headers for the Cloudflare (Sites) deployment.
#
# Assets are served by the Workers assets binding *before* the Next.js worker
# sees the request, so `next.config.ts` `headers()` never runs for them. The
# document itself is Cross-Origin Isolated (`Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy:
# require-corp`), which the browser-local WASM OCR and PDF pipelines need; a
# nested worker script fetched from an isolated document must carry the same
# policy or Chrome refuses it with `net::ERR_BLOCKED_BY_RESPONSE` and OCR dies
# before tesseract starts. These rules give the worker scripts the same
# isolation policy the page has.
#
# Verified against `wrangler dev` (workerd): with these rules the OCR guard
# worker spawns, loads the WASM core and language data, and recognizes text.
#
# Keep the framework cache rule in sync with the Sites build output.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=31536000,immutable

# Unversioned worker assets: NOT immutable.
#
# The URLs are fixed while the copied package files change on an upgrade, so
# `immutable` would let a browser keep an old tesseract worker/WASM core (or
# PDF.js worker) for a year and pair it with a new page bundle. One hour bounds
# that skew; `must-revalidate` prevents a stale response after the window.
# The identical policy is emitted by next.config.ts `headers()` for Node hosts.
# `/tesseract/eng.traineddata.gz` is not an asset and does not match this rule:
# it is rewritten to /api/ocr-model, whose response is digest-pinned and keeps
# its own one-year `immutable` header.
#
# Compression is left to the host: Cloudflare's assets binding negotiates
# Brotli/gzip for JavaScript. Do not add `Content-Encoding` (it would suppress
# or double-apply compression) or `no-transform` (it forbids compression).
/tesseract/*
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=3600,must-revalidate

/pdf.worker.min.mjs
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=3600,must-revalidate
